      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C67","C68","C70","C71","C74","C75","C76","C77"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule; the decision relies on transfer from analog contexts.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability data are available; L6 records are for imipramine/desipramine and other analogs, not the query.",
    "No query-specific intestinal permeability, efflux, or metabolism data are available; L4/L5 records are analog-based, and the query is fully ionized at physiological pH.",
    "No human oral F values for imipramine/desipramine are supplied, so their high hepatic intrinsic clearance cannot be directly threshold-calibrated to F<20%.",
    "L3 AUC/Cmax records lack IV comparators and cannot independently establish absolute F.",
    "The alfentanil context contains a conflicting 1% F record (C13), adding uncertainty to that analog."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F>=20%) remains best supported: human amitriptyline and alfentanil F values (30-60% and 37-45%) and essentially complete absorption/high permeability of close basic-amine analogs outweigh L6 high hepatic intrinsic clearance, which indicates first-pass loss but is not threshold-determinative and is not accompanied by a direct low F for the query. Confidence lowered to low because L6 adds a negative mechanistic factor and all evidence is transferred."
}

